@page "/deployment-overview"

<PageTitle>Deployment Overview - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="operations-dashboard deployment-overview-page">
    <PageIntro Eyebrow="Production Planning"
               Title="Deployment Overview"
               Subtitle="A production-aware overview of how OperationsFlow could move from a local Blazor prototype into a hosted, monitored, backed-up, supportable internal business system.">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="implementation-plan">Implementation Plan</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="prototype-scope">Prototype Scope</a>
    </PageIntro>

    <div class="page-purpose-note">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> use this page to explain what would need to change before OperationsFlow could be deployed for real users. The current prototype runs locally with demo data. A production rollout would need hosted infrastructure, secure configuration, environment separation, database hosting, backups, monitoring, release checks, and support planning.
    </div>

    <section class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Current Hosting</span>
            <strong>Local</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Portfolio demo environment</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Production Target</span>
            <strong>Hosted</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Controlled business deployment</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Database Target</span>
            <strong>SQL</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Hosted storage with backups</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Release Need</span>
            <strong>Pipeline</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Build, test, deploy, monitor</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid deployment-intro-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Deployment Summary</h2>
                    <p>How the prototype would become a live internal system.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="deployment-copy">
                OperationsFlow currently proves the workflow, page structure, data model, reporting views, and production planning.
                To become a live business system, it would need to move from local demo hosting into a controlled deployment environment.
                That means replacing local demo storage, adding secure configuration, separating development/test/production environments,
                backing up data, monitoring errors, and creating a safe release process.
            </p>

            <ul class="action-list">
                <li>Move from local demo hosting to a controlled hosted environment.</li>
                <li>Replace local SQLite/demo storage with production database storage.</li>
                <li>Separate development, testing, staging, and production configuration.</li>
                <li>Add backup, restore, monitoring, logging, and support processes.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Prototype Boundary</h2>
                    <p>What the current project is not pretending to have.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="deployment-boundary-highlight">
                <span>Prototype boundary</span>
                <strong>Not deployed as production yet</strong>
                <p>
                    The current build is a local portfolio prototype. It is not a live production service yet.
                    A production version would need hosted infrastructure, secure identity, production database storage,
                    backup routines, release controls, monitoring, and support documentation.
                </p>
            </div>

            <ol class="action-list">
                <li>Choose a production hosting target.</li>
                <li>Move data to hosted storage.</li>
                <li>Add authentication and configuration controls.</li>
                <li>Create deployment and rollback steps.</li>
                <li>Monitor errors, uptime, and workflow health.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deployment-card-grid">
        @foreach (var item in DeploymentAreas)
        {
            <article class="deployment-card">
                <div class="deployment-card-header">
                    <span>@item.Number</span>
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">@item.Category</p>
                        <h2>@item.Title</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <p>@item.Description</p>

                <div class="deployment-state-box">
                    <span>Current prototype</span>
                    <strong>@item.CurrentState</strong>
                </div>

                <div class="deployment-state-box production">
                    <span>Production target</span>
                    <strong>@item.ProductionTarget</strong>
                </div>
            </article>
        }
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Deployment Readiness Matrix</h2>
                <p>What exists now, what is missing, and what would be needed before a real rollout.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table deployment-readiness-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Area</th>
                    <th>Prototype State</th>
                    <th>Production Requirement</th>
                    <th>Recommended Upgrade</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var item in ReadinessItems)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@item.Area</strong></td>
                        <td><span class="@item.BadgeClass">@item.PrototypeState</span></td>
                        <td>@item.ProductionRequirement</td>
                        <td>@item.RecommendedUpgrade</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Environment Flow</h2>
                    <p>How changes should move safely toward production.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="environment-flow-list">
                @foreach (var step in EnvironmentFlow)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@step.Number</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong>@step.Title</strong>
                            <p>@step.Description</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Hosting Options</h2>
                    <p>Possible production deployment approaches.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="hosting-option-grid">
                @foreach (var option in HostingOptions)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@option.Label</span>
                        <strong>@option.Title</strong>
                        <p>@option.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Production Deployment Checklist</h2>
                <p>A practical checklist for turning the prototype into a controlled internal business app.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table deployment-checklist-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Step</th>
                    <th>What To Confirm</th>
                    <th>Why It Matters</th>
                    <th>Status</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var item in ChecklistItems)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@item.Step</strong></td>
                        <td>@item.WhatToConfirm</td>
                        <td>@item.WhyItMatters</td>
                        <td><span class="@item.BadgeClass">@item.Status</span></td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Release Pipeline</h2>
                    <p>How updates should be built, checked, and released.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <ol class="demo-step-list deployment-pipeline-list">
                <li>
                    <strong>Build the app</strong>
                    <span>Compile the project and confirm the release build succeeds.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Run automated checks</strong>
                    <span>Run unit tests, page checks, data quality checks, and workflow validation where available.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Deploy to test/staging</strong>
                    <span>Use a non-production environment to confirm the release works with realistic configuration.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Approve production release</strong>
                    <span>Confirm the release owner, deployment notes, rollback plan, and support contact.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Monitor after release</strong>
                    <span>Watch logs, errors, uptime, performance, and user-reported issues after deployment.</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Operational Support</h2>
                    <p>What happens after deployment.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="support-grid">
                @foreach (var item in SupportItems)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@item.Label</span>
                        <strong>@item.Title</strong>
                        <p>@item.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Risk And Control Map</h2>
                <p>Deployment risks and the controls that would reduce them.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table deployment-risk-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Risk</th>
                    <th>Example Problem</th>
                    <th>Control</th>
                    <th>Review Question</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var item in RiskItems)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@item.Risk</strong></td>
                        <td>@item.ExampleProblem</td>
                        <td>@item.Control</td>
                        <td>@item.ReviewQuestion</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Low-Risk First Deployment</h2>
                    <p>The safest rollout path for this kind of system.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="first-deployment-list">
                @foreach (var item in FirstDeploymentSteps)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@item.Number</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong>@item.Title</strong>
                            <p>@item.Description</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>What This Proves</h2>
                    <p>The portfolio value of deployment planning.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="deployment-proof-grid">
                @foreach (var proof in ProofItems)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@proof.Label</span>
                        <strong>@proof.Title</strong>
                        <p>@proof.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card deployment-summary-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Deployment Overview Summary</h2>
                <p>A short explanation for reviewers.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="deployment-summary-copy">
            <p>
                OperationsFlow is currently a local Blazor/.NET portfolio prototype. It demonstrates the workflow model,
                user interface, data model, reporting views, traceability concepts, role planning, and production-awareness needed
                for an internal business system.
            </p>

            <p>
                A production deployment would require secure hosting, authenticated users, hosted database storage, backups,
                environment separation, configuration management, release pipelines, rollback planning, monitoring, logging,
                support documentation, and controlled pilot rollout. This page shows that the project has been designed with
                realistic deployment and support requirements in mind, not just local demo screens.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

